From: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:52:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm: zte: add support for ZTE Sanechips ZX279125 and VSOL V2801SG

This commit adds board support for the V-SOL V2801SG GPON ONT powered by
the ZTE Sanechips ZX279125 dual-core ARMv7 Cortex-A9 SoC, including:
- Architecture and platform defconfig
- Serial UART driver (zx279125_uart)
- Hardware Timer / clocksource (zx279125_timer)
- SPI NOR controller driver (zx279125_spifc) with ZB25VQ64 detection
- Gigabit Ethernet MAC / Packet Processor DMA driver (zx279125_eth)
- The low 16 MiB managed by U-Boot, retaining the hardware packet pool
- Environment in SPI flash (usercfg partition at 0x7a0000)

Signed-off-by: Ifran Ali <khanu.i.i.k.2000@gmail.com>
---
